# The runtime dependencies as a user's install resolves them today, for the
# Security workflow's dependency audit. python/pyproject.toml asks for
# mcp>=2.0, pyOpenVBA>=6.3.3,<7, pyOfficeEditor>=0.4.1,<0.5 and
# pyvbaanalysis>=2.3.1,<3; this pins the release of each that PyPI serves
# now, and Dependabot moves the pins daily (the owner's packages skip the
# cooldown), so the audit follows what a fresh install gets. image.txt and
# test.txt pin the versions the image and the conformance corpus run, which
# can trail these by a release. Compiled for the oldest Python the package
# supports:
#   uv pip compile runtime.in --universal --generate-hashes --python-version 3.10 -o runtime.txt
mcp==2.2.0
pyopenvba==6.5.0
pyofficeeditor==0.4.1
pyvbaanalysis==2.3.1
